From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:43:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] aarch64: disable separate shrink-wrapping for SEH
 targets

Separate shrink-wrapping saves and restores individual callee-saved
registers on the paths that need them, outside the prologue.  Windows
ARM64 unwind data describes a single prologue, so this cannot be
expressed; the restores in the function body were instead emitted as
.seh_save_reg.  When the offset is misaligned or out of range the
assembler rejects them:

  Error: offset should be a multiple of 8
  Error: offset overflows expected range

and otherwise accepts them as wrong unwind data.

Return NULL from aarch64_get_separate_components for SEH targets, the
standard way to opt out (try_shrink_wrapping_separate stops when there
are no components).  Ordinary shrink-wrapping of the whole prologue is
unaffected.

Signed-off-by: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
---
 gcc/config/aarch64/aarch64.cc | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/config/aarch64/aarch64.cc b/gcc/config/aarch64/aarch64.cc
index 2d08d1a..2906296 100644
--- a/gcc/config/aarch64/aarch64.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/aarch64/aarch64.cc
@@ -10021,6 +10021,16 @@ offset_12bit_unsigned_scaled_p (machine_mode mode, poly_int64 offset)
 static sbitmap
 aarch64_get_separate_components (void)
 {
+#ifdef TARGET_SEH
+  /* Windows unwind data describes a single prologue: the SEH directives
+     only express register saves made before .seh_endprologue.  Separate
+     shrink-wrapping moves individual saves and restores into the body, where
+     they are reported as saves with offsets the assembler rejects or, worse,
+     accepts.  */
+  if (TARGET_SEH)
+    return NULL;
+#endif
+
   aarch64_frame &frame = cfun->machine->frame;
   sbitmap components = sbitmap_alloc (LAST_SAVED_REGNUM + 1);
   bitmap_clear (components);
